WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:04.530
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.530 --> 00:08.170
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.170 --> 00:16.100
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.250 --> 00:27.760
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.760 --> 00:33.700
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.700 --> 00:42.640
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.640 --> 00:47.410
Like the wind

00:47.410 --> 00:50.480
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.480 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.520
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.520 --> 01:07.330
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.330 --> 01:13.440
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.440 --> 01:20.180
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.180 --> 01:27.410
The roadless journey continues

01:38.290 --> 01:40.780
What to do?

01:42.800 --> 01:46.570
I mean, we are going to go that way, but...

01:46.570 --> 01:49.500
There's something we have to take care of first.

01:54.580 --> 01:58.180
That's fine for us, but...

01:58.180 --> 02:00.480
The problem is how to feed this guy.

02:02.850 --> 02:06.450
Besides, always having to
camp out like this is just...

02:06.450 --> 02:09.720
I'd like to take a shower for once.

02:09.720 --> 02:12.230
But how to earn the money...

02:12.230 --> 02:14.590
You're a bounty hunter, aren't you?

02:21.240 --> 02:23.570
Well, yeah, but...

02:26.880 --> 02:29.680
Nadie is a bounty hunter.

02:29.680 --> 02:34.380
That was true in the past
and is also true in the present.

03:10.920 --> 03:15.520
They're all called bounties,
but there are all kinds of scenarios.

03:24.600 --> 03:26.630
The most common scenario...

03:26.630 --> 03:31.410
...is where the guy is out on bail with
money borrowed from a bond agent,

03:31.410 --> 03:34.980
and decides to go on the lam.

03:34.980 --> 03:38.710
Sometimes, the victim's family puts
a price on the perpetrator's head.

03:42.450 --> 03:44.550
In the case of large incidents like terrorism,

03:44.550 --> 03:46.780
the government sometimes sets prices, too.

04:13.250 --> 04:18.490
The easiest and least troublesome
are the bounties of the underworld.

04:18.490 --> 04:20.720
Why?

04:20.720 --> 04:22.310
Bang.

04:23.630 --> 04:27.030
I'm "bang," too.

04:27.030 --> 04:29.400
I want some quick and easy cash.

04:29.400 --> 04:30.800
In what amount?

04:30.800 --> 04:32.960
The more, the better.

04:36.570 --> 04:38.670
One that's close to here,

04:38.670 --> 04:41.480
whose general location is already known,

04:41.480 --> 04:44.650
and has the highest price on his head...

04:44.650 --> 04:46.550
...is this guy.

04:46.550 --> 04:50.790
The fee for the intel is 5%.

04:50.790 --> 04:52.580
Okay.

04:57.560 --> 05:00.650
5% for that level of bounty is too much!

05:08.800 --> 05:10.570
We're in the clear now.

05:12.870 --> 05:15.080
I'll be damned if we run out
of gas or have to camp out,

05:15.080 --> 05:17.650
so let's put all our effort into this search.

05:17.650 --> 05:19.410
Yessir.

05:42.900 --> 05:46.070
I see, so they did appear.

05:46.070 --> 05:48.010
I'll meet up with you right away.

05:52.880 --> 05:55.450
Aren't you getting tired of this already?

05:55.450 --> 05:57.650
It's supposedly good for dieting.

06:19.970 --> 06:22.440
Then, good luck to you.

06:26.710 --> 06:28.620
It'll be fine.

06:28.620 --> 06:30.850
There'll be no more camping out.

06:33.690 --> 06:35.820
The target's name is Guerrero.

06:35.820 --> 06:38.890
He made off with money that
belonged to an organization.

06:38.890 --> 06:40.800
The story is that a month ago,

06:40.800 --> 06:44.870
he was apparently looking
for a house around here.

06:44.870 --> 06:46.860
What fine information that is.

06:59.550 --> 07:03.990
But it's not entirely
useless information, either.

07:03.990 --> 07:09.460
If he was looking for a house,
it means he thought this town was safe.

07:09.460 --> 07:14.160
And when a fugitive feels a place is safe,

07:14.160 --> 07:17.860
he will continue to remain there
as long as nothing changes.

07:19.930 --> 07:22.600
So, he could still be around...

07:24.440 --> 07:28.040
- What is it?
- You've given this some serious thought.

07:28.040 --> 07:30.550
Well, yeah, I'm a pro at this.

07:30.550 --> 07:33.010
Oh, right.

07:33.010 --> 07:37.210
If things change, you run away.

08:08.950 --> 08:10.990
Wh-What the hell?!

08:10.990 --> 08:13.920
Take me to your immediate boss.

08:17.860 --> 08:19.960
What these guys don't want...

08:19.960 --> 08:24.590
...is to have bounty hunters
swaggering about their turf.

08:33.270 --> 08:36.680
So this is where he got his face changed.

08:36.680 --> 08:39.150
You should get plastic surgery, too.

08:40.950 --> 08:42.680
Same to you, too.

08:42.680 --> 08:45.820
We need to get back to work...

08:45.820 --> 08:48.190
Yes, thanks for your cooperation.

08:48.190 --> 08:50.290
I'm sure you know this,

08:50.290 --> 08:53.560
but you never met either of us.

08:53.560 --> 08:55.600
You two were out for a walk.

08:55.600 --> 08:57.900
What about our faces?!

08:57.900 --> 09:00.770
Why don't you just say
you had a friendly fistfight?

09:02.140 --> 09:04.130
What the heck does that mean?

09:08.640 --> 09:10.840
Pardon me...

10:08.670 --> 10:11.670
Nadie.

10:11.670 --> 10:13.370
Why?

10:22.350 --> 10:24.320
I-I don't know anything.

10:24.320 --> 10:28.090
Really, I didn't know anything.

10:28.090 --> 10:30.390
An unsurprising response.

10:30.390 --> 10:33.360
When you're in this kind of business,

10:33.360 --> 10:36.200
if you pry too much into people's private lives,

10:36.200 --> 10:38.700
it could very well cost you your own life.

10:38.700 --> 10:43.240
So you don't ask any questions.
You make no inquiries.

10:43.240 --> 10:46.240
You just treat the patients that turn up.

10:46.240 --> 10:48.840
We know that as well as you do.

10:48.840 --> 10:51.980
So we only have one question for you.

10:51.980 --> 10:55.280
What does his face look like now?

10:55.280 --> 10:58.020
I don't know.

10:58.020 --> 10:59.720
I don't remember.

10:59.720 --> 11:03.120
Want me to change your face, too?

11:03.120 --> 11:07.900
There might be nothing left
of its original shape, though.

11:07.900 --> 11:11.760
If you have any last words, say them now.

11:20.140 --> 11:25.170
Right. His eyes are like this
actor's and he has a sharp nose.

11:30.750 --> 11:33.290
What?! 3%?!

11:33.290 --> 11:34.960
Yeah.

11:34.960 --> 11:39.890
That bastard. He told me
the intel would cost me 5%.

11:39.890 --> 11:42.030
Ticks me off!

11:42.030 --> 11:44.300
That's the difference in experience.

11:44.300 --> 11:51.240
I used to be a pretty well-known
bounty hunter up north myself.

11:51.240 --> 11:57.480
How about 50/50? We both want
cash as soon as possible, right?

11:57.480 --> 12:01.480
- 60/40.
- 50/50.

12:01.480 --> 12:03.950
Let's go, Lirio.

12:06.850 --> 12:08.790
Lirio...

12:11.190 --> 12:13.060
50/50 it is.

12:28.010 --> 12:30.770
How's it going, Doug? Catch anything?

12:42.960 --> 12:44.930
The secret to fishing, you see...

12:44.930 --> 12:46.490
I didn't realize you were awake.

12:46.490 --> 12:50.230
...is to wait patiently until
you've caught your prey.

12:50.230 --> 12:52.000
Is that true?

12:52.000 --> 12:53.760
It's true.

12:58.210 --> 13:00.780
See? I caught you.

13:00.780 --> 13:02.370
Oh, Doug.

14:17.950 --> 14:21.590
Living in a luxury condo with
the money he ran off with...

14:21.590 --> 14:24.930
He sure is living it up.

14:24.930 --> 14:27.620
We just have to wait for now.

14:30.160 --> 14:31.470
We do?

14:31.470 --> 14:35.070
The security looks pretty tight anyway.

14:35.070 --> 14:37.400
I guess we're in the car again tonight.

14:52.250 --> 14:55.620
Wiñay Marka...

14:55.620 --> 14:59.120
If something were to happen to me,
could you make it there by yourself?

15:03.060 --> 15:06.190
Be prepared to do that if
the worst should happen.

15:48.410 --> 15:50.040
That sound just now...

15:50.040 --> 15:51.530
Ricardo!

16:11.030 --> 16:12.570
I am taking Ellis into custody.

16:12.570 --> 16:14.260
Wait.

16:20.640 --> 16:22.730
Are you a bounty hunter?!

16:25.110 --> 16:27.170
Do you suppose it's from Guerrero's room?

16:43.730 --> 16:45.430
I'll approach from above!

16:45.430 --> 16:47.560
Then I'll approach from below!

16:53.710 --> 16:55.400
No.

17:06.150 --> 17:07.780
Ellis...

17:10.620 --> 17:14.360
You need him, don't you?

17:14.360 --> 17:17.360
I'll bring him down for you.

17:17.360 --> 17:19.060
No.

17:22.140 --> 17:23.800
Ellis...

17:49.700 --> 17:51.460
Guerrero!

18:06.480 --> 18:07.680
Ellis!

18:07.680 --> 18:09.770
Out of my way!

18:21.160 --> 18:24.190
Are you all right?! Ellis?! Lirio?!

18:41.620 --> 18:43.350
Nadie...

18:43.350 --> 18:47.750
Hand... over... that car!

18:59.200 --> 19:00.720
Nadie!

19:04.770 --> 19:06.470
Nadie...

19:10.480 --> 19:13.350
Ow, that hurt...

19:13.350 --> 19:15.250
I slipped.

19:19.350 --> 19:23.260
Huh? Is it over already?

19:23.260 --> 19:25.790
What?! It's frozen!

19:25.790 --> 19:27.560
How?!

19:48.380 --> 19:52.650
I got scolded by Ellis again.

19:57.690 --> 20:00.720
I look forward to doing business with you again.

20:09.900 --> 20:11.670
Here's your share.

20:11.670 --> 20:14.310
All right!

20:14.310 --> 20:19.450
One, two, three, four, five...

20:19.450 --> 20:24.280
...six, seven, eight, nine, ten...

20:24.280 --> 20:27.250
Wasn't our deal half?

20:27.250 --> 20:31.490
If you'd gone, he would've
taken a 5% commission.

20:31.490 --> 20:33.290
Cheapskate.

20:33.290 --> 20:36.300
Neither of us can afford
to fritter our money away.

20:36.300 --> 20:38.560
Yeah, that's true, but...

20:40.670 --> 20:42.460
This is from Lirio.

20:49.710 --> 20:51.540
Ricardo...

21:03.360 --> 21:06.630
Woohoo, a full tank for once!

21:06.630 --> 21:08.730
Well, let's meet again if luck would have it.

21:08.730 --> 21:10.420
Sure.

21:16.640 --> 21:18.430
Do they worry you?

21:23.310 --> 21:25.010
Yeah...

21:25.010 --> 21:27.710
You can't defy destiny.

21:35.860 --> 21:37.720
Nadie.

21:39.630 --> 21:42.630
So you were...

21:42.630 --> 21:45.890
...always doing this sort of thing...

21:48.840 --> 21:51.530
Since before you met me...

21:55.610 --> 21:57.370
I suppose.

22:01.350 --> 22:03.010
I'll...

22:06.690 --> 22:08.420
...never...

22:10.420 --> 22:12.720
...suggest it again.

22:16.960 --> 22:18.760
Yessir.

22:24.040 --> 22:28.440
Danger is the constant
companion of bounty hunters.

22:28.440 --> 22:33.640
And Nadie is no exception.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Like flowers that never die

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
A night of red stars

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
The vanishing warmth

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
I want to keep it here

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
You, with your eyes closed

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Yearning over and over

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
...everything
